-…, BLOCK, 4 blockers): addressed the round-1 findings (boolean-emitting engine_route step; regenerated config docs + golden in Scope; produce_plan_review_verdict engine defaults to \"pipeline\"), plus an env exclusion because ADR 0123 rules out an env var and every _SECTIONS key gets REBAR_<SECTION>_<KEY> automatically. Round-2 blockers, each verified against the tree: (1) the mechanism-ok marker must sit above the _SECTIONS entry in _config_sections.py (markers.py:76-83 harvests only that line or the one above), not in _config_schema.py; (2-4) the env exclusion missed other canonical-env enumerations: test_gen_env_registry.py:302, generate_config_surface_golden.py:49-53, test_config_surface_golden.py:39, config.py:381. Round 3 revision moves the marker and adds one helper env_overridable_keys() used by all of those sites. Re-review started: job 1794364527945316669-2d9bce72d3b545a0af501eb372b899ad.","timestamp":1794364544367272138},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Round 3 (job 1794364527945316669-…) BLOCK, 3 blockers, all the same defect, verified at __init__.py:472-500: reuse.idempotent_reuse, reuse.verdict_reuse and orchestrator.drift_refresh return before dispatch and ignore the engine, so \"agentic\" could return a reused or re-signed pipeline verdict or make pipeline LLM calls. Round 4 revision: thread engine into _run_plan_review (call at :273) and add `engine == \"pipeline\" and` to each of the 3 existing conditions (measured: ruff counts no complexity for boolean operands, so _run_plan_review stays at 17 against its ceiling 19); tests for the 3 shortcut cases. Re-review started.","timestamp":1794365328636055478},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-10 19:00 PST: OPEN, CLAIM-READY. Round-4 plan review PASS, certified at 91182f96362 (job 1794365328502139759-1ae4c2f6798746fba37fd0e0f9e664d2). Not implemented and not claimed. Description 7,978 chars; file_impact updated to the 22 Scope paths. Round history: r1 BLOCK (expression grammar, generated docs, produce_plan_review_verdict default); r2 BLOCK (marker placement, env-name enumerations); r3 BLOCK (reuse/drift-refresh shortcuts ignore engine); r4 PASS. Next: claim, then implement in a worktree at origin/main. If main moves before the claim, check currency with `rebar review-plan skilled-cepevorous-naga --status`. Any description edit stales the cert.","timestamp":1794365983895512405},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress 2026-11-11 PST: claimed (cert current, verified via review-plan --status from a worktree at origin/main b878c4be768). Implemented in worktree engine-switch, local commit d5bb898ab6b; make verify next, then Gerrit push.\n\nOne deviation from the plan text, needed to meet AC2 (zero LLM calls under \"agentic\"): besides the 3 pipeline-only shortcuts, the post-dispatch tail (rising/completion/drift floors, xcheck, fix-unit grouping) also makes LLM sub-calls. Measured: with a drift-stale attestation, drift_floor.maybe_apply ran a novelty call on the degraded agentic INDETERMINATE. That tail is extracted into _apply_review_floors and skipped when engine != \"pipeline\" and the verdict is llm_unavailable (the failed agentic run); a floor short-circuit still gets the identical tail under both engines. _run_plan_review complexity 18 (ceiling 19), __init__.py 695 LOC.\n\nTest note: a DET verdict with 2+ blockers makes the pre-existing fix-unit grouping call under BOTH engines (identical); the floor-blocked test uses a single-blocker plan so its zero-call assertion holds.","timestamp":1794424582842104151}],"created_at":1794255849014187001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bc273803-0d5a-4a13-a6cc-6255e2f23bc0","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"11f7-cf57-be02-4441"},{"link_uuid":"6d5be30b-cf7e-4bed-83d8-e7b88ed597e8","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7341-7f22-b13a-442c"},{"link_uuid":"3961ba85-d0e4-4c19-80c5-a1ddb988b28b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3a03-d968-518b-4a8a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe epic needs one option selecting the plan-review engine (pipeline or agentic) so both can run on one ticket. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml` has no selection point today.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Key.** Add the key ADR 0123 records, `[verify] plan_review_engine`, values `\"pipeline\"` and `\"agentic\"`, default `\"pipeline\"`. Declare it in `src/rebar/_config_schema.py` beside `require_plan_review_for_close` (line 71) as `plan_review_engine: str = _documented(\"pipeline\", ...)`, and validate it in `src/rebar/_config_sections.py`'s `_SECTIONS[\"verify\"]` with the existing `_as_choice(v, k, {\"pipeline\", \"agentic\"})` (pattern at line 95), so an unknown configured value is a config error at load time. `# mechanism-ok: config_key verify.plan_review_engine — bossy-impish-hoiho` sits directly above that `_SECTIONS` entry (the detector reads only that line and the one above, `scripts/_mechanism_delta/markers.py:76-83`), as at line 92.\n\n**No env var.** ADR 0123 forbids one, but every `_SECTIONS` key gets `REBAR_<SECTION>_<KEY>` automatically. `_config_sources.py` adds `_ENV_EXCLUDED_KEYS = frozenset({(\"verify\", \"plan_review_engine\")})` and helper `env_overridable_keys()` (each `_SECTIONS` pair not in it). Every canonical-env enumeration switches to it: `env_overrides` (`_config_sources.py:331`), the config cache signature (`config.py:381`), `scripts/gen_env_registry.py:409`, `scripts/generate_config_surface_golden.py:49-53`, and the derived-set tests `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:302` and `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py:39`. So `REBAR_VERIFY_PLAN_REVIEW_ENGINE` is never read, documented or expected; the sunset ticket removes the entry.\n\n**Resolution.** `review_plan` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:199`) gains a keyword `engine: str | None = None`. Precedence per the ADR: an explicit argument, else the config key, else `\"pipeline\"`. An explicit value outside the two names raises `ConfigError` naming it before any store read or LLM call. CLI/MCP flags belong to the surfaces ticket.\n\n**Dispatch.** `review_plan` passes the resolved value to `_run_plan_review` (call at `__init__.py:273`, which gains an `engine` keyword). `gate_dispatch.produce_plan_review_verdict` (`gate_dispatch.py:66`) gains `engine: str = \"pipeline\"`, mirroring `overlap: bool = False` (line 75), always placed in the `run_workflow` inputs (line 191); `_run_plan_review` passes it at line 522. Existing callers and tests keep the default.\n\n**Pipeline-only shortcuts.** Three steps in `_run_plan_review` return before dispatch and are pipeline-attestation based: `reuse.idempotent_reuse` (line 473), `reuse.verdict_reuse` (line 480) and `orchestrator.drift_refresh` (line 490, whose probe calls `produce_plan_review_verdict` at `orchestrator.py:499` and re-signs). Each existing `if` gains `engine == \"pipeline\" and`, so under `\"agentic\"` none can return a reused or re-signed pipeline verdict or make a pipeline LLM call. Boolean operands add no McCabe branch (`_run_plan_review` stays 17, ceiling 19).\n\n**Workflow selection.** The v3 expression grammar accepts only single references (`lint_expr.py`; no `==`/`&&`), so a deterministic step computes it, like `grounding` → `code_grounded`:\n\n- `plan-review.yaml` declares input `engine` (string, default `\"pipeline\"`).\n- New top-level step `engine_route` (`needs: [precheck]`) uses new scripted op `plan_review_engine_route` in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py`, inputs `run_llm: ${{ steps.precheck.outputs.run_llm }}` and `engine: ${{ inputs.engine }}`. It emits one boolean, `run_pipeline = run_llm and engine == \"pipeline\"`.\n- The `review` branch (line 56) changes its condition from `steps.precheck.outputs.run_llm` to `${{ steps.engine_route.outputs.run_pipeline }}` and gains `engine_route` in `needs`. Its `then` arm and its `else` passthrough arm are unchanged.\n\n**Floor first, no silent passthrough.** Not-claimable tickets fast-fail at `__init__.py:398-400`; a floor block or exempt type sets `run_llm` false, so the passthrough emits the precheck verdict under both values, byte-identical, no LLM call. With `run_llm` true and `\"agentic\"`, `plan_review_engine_route` raises naming the value (engine not yet available); the failed run takes the existing failed-run path to an unsigned INDETERMINATE carrying that error, never a passthrough verdict. The agentic-engine ticket replaces the raise with its arm.\n\n## Scope\n\n- rebar.toml (`[verify] plan_review_engine = \"pipeline\"`, commented)\n- src/rebar/_config_schema.py (field)\n- src/rebar/_config_sections.py (validation + marker)\n- src/rebar/_config_sources.py (`_ENV_EXCLUDED_KEYS`, `env_overridable_keys`)\n- src/rebar/config.py (cache signature loop)\n- scripts/gen_env_registry.py, scripts/generate_config_surface_golden.py, tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py, tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py (use the helper)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py (engine argument, resolution, shortcut guards)\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py (`engine` keyword; 778 lines, adds under 10)\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml (input, `engine_route`, condition)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py (`plan_review_engine_route` op)\n- src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_engine_route_input.schema.json (new)\n- src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_engine_route_output.schema.json (new)\n- src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py (register beside `plan_review_grounding`, line 289)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_workflow_ops_seam.py (`_EXPECTED_OPS` gains the new op)\n- docs/config.md (narrative entry for the key)\n- docs/config-reference.md, docs/env-vars.md, tests/golden/config_surface.json (regenerated)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: no key or `\"pipeline\"` runs the pipeline; explicit `engine=\"pipeline\"` beats a configured `\"agentic\"`; `produce_plan_review_verdict` defaults the input to `\"pipeline\"`.\n- Shortcuts: with a valid pipeline attestation, with a stored matching BLOCK, and with a code-drift-only stale attestation, `engine=\"agentic\"` (`sign=True`) still returns the unsigned INDETERMINATE with zero LLM calls; under `\"pipeline\"` each shortcut still fires.\n- Route op: `run_pipeline` true only for `run_llm=true, engine=\"pipeline\"`; false when `run_llm=false` under both; raises naming the value for `run_llm=true, engine=\"agentic\"`.\n- Env: `REBAR_VERIFY_PLAN_REVIEW_ENGINE=agentic` exported, no key: engine stays `\"pipeline\"`; env-vars doc and golden omit the name.\n- Failure/edge: unknown configured value → load error naming it; unknown argument → `ConfigError`, zero LLM calls; floor-blocked and not-claimable tickets: zero LLM calls under both values (`FakeRunner`, `runner.py:194`, call counts), identical verdict and findings; DET-passing under `\"agentic\"` → unsigned INDETERMINATE naming the engine, never the passthrough verdict.\n- The gate workflow lints clean.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `[verify] plan_review_engine` is read with default `\"pipeline\"`, explicit-argument precedence, no environment override, and an error on unknown configured or explicit values; pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py`.\n- [ ] Floor-blocked and not-claimable reviews make zero LLM calls and return identical results under both values, and a DET-passing review under `\"agentic\"` returns an unsigned INDETERMINATE naming the engine with zero LLM calls, including when a valid, BLOCK-reusable or drift-stale pipeline attestation exists; pinned by call-counting tests in the same file.\n- [ ] `produce_plan_review_verdict` defaults `engine` to `\"pipeline\"`, so the drift-refresh probe and existing callers are unchanged; pinned by a test asserting the workflow input.\n- [ ] `docs/config-reference.md`, `docs/env-vars.md` and `tests/golden/config_surface.json` are regenerated and their drift checks pass.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0 with the marker naming the open sunset ticket.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"rebar.toml","reason":"plan_review_engine key"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"field"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reason":"validation + mechanism marker"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sources.py","reason":"env exclusion + env_overridable_keys"},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"cache signature loop"},{"path":"scripts/gen_env_registry.py","reason":"use helper"},{"path":"scripts/generate_config_surface_golden.py","reason":"use helper"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py","reason":"derived set uses helper"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py","reason":"derived set uses helper"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"engine argument and resolution"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"engine workflow input"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml","reason":"engine input, engine_route step, review condition"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"plan_review_engine_route op"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_engine_route_input.schema.json","reason":"new op input contract"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_engine_route_output.schema.json","reason":"new op output contract"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py","reason":"register op schemas"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_workflow_ops_seam.py","reason":"expected ops census"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"key documented"},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"tests/golden/config_surface.json","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["depends_on","11f7-cf57-be02-4441"],["depends_on","7341-7f22-b13a-442c"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","3a03-d968-518b-4a8a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"e45b1787-28e2-4e5a-ab5d-9f43d1b42021","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2886-3079-9b31-4838","ticket_type":"story","title":"Plan-review engine switch: [verify] plan_review_engine, dispatched after the Layer-1 floor","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d15026e4-03ad-4028-85e4-ff3f17e72dcb","c8cb7b9f-9884-4070-a19b-808f3d8da627","b10870a1-f15d-44e9-8502-5bbee15efcab","f58d0aaf-fc5d-4d96-b7c3-87581280640a","3baecc90-647a-466e-a10c-c8b01f3113e2","5737fbc6-fafb-4869-bc23-85cd3331a350","5953ad00-954d-45d5-8a47-b25a14797929","83701199-a76a-4f03-bf11-4b43dc6a0b88","4655b321-bee1-4eb2-9fc2-566e26a48750","68e683b7-ab6d-486f-94a9-f9400e2c287b","e45b1787-28e2-4e5a-ab5d-9f43d1b42021","1fe0c092-66b8-47f6-a34a-474ca9f3eb34","5743098c-3867-420c-b43a-d00513a69847","3961ba85-d0e4-4c19-80c5-a1ddb988b28b"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794428064951956640,"uuid":"e7bd96d3-e331-4b7e-886d-8a7086cc25b9"}